From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Astall <aa@clhoz.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] game: add Twelve Minutes profile with a 2 GB pool

Twelve Minutes 1.0.1 (0100CD701434C000): Unity 2019.4.31f1 IL2CPP with
FMOD, SDK 12.3.7. The profile is the NSP script's provisional one with
app_pool cut from the Switch's 3285 MB to 2 GB.

nninitStartup hands pool minus used memory to StandardAllocator. With
the Switch's pool that region is 3.14 GB, and Unity's own regions above
it reach +4.26 GB of the iPhone's 4.38 GB alias region at the end of the
first load. A texture then reads a pool pointer of floats and the host
crashes in nvn_sparse_pool. With 2 GB, 130 s on the Mac with the
iPhone's alias size end at +3.51 GB, 2.27 GB mapped, no crash.

Checked on an iPhone (past the first load) and on the Mac (title prompt
and opening credits). Later chapters were not played.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2904
Reason: Twelve Minutes needs a 2 GB pool to fit the iPhone alias region; bridge until upstream merges
Issue: none (seedds/nxnative#217)

